close_reason: fixed
body: "The /healthz handler was a constant shaped like a probe: it returned { ok: true, version } regardless of whether any dependency was reachable. Docker and monitoring polled it and saw green during a real outage. The fix probes the real PostgreSQL pool (SELECT 1, not a fresh connection — pool exhaustion is itself a failure mode), the projects root (write-and-remove a temp file inside it — a missing or read-only host mount is the exact failure caught), and soft dependencies (Neo4j, Ollama) when configured. Every probe is bounded to 2s. The computed result is cached for 5s. The response is backward compatible: ok and version remain top-level; a per-dependency breakdown is added. Tests drive every failure path with a real temp directory and stub pools, and non-vacuity checks prove each test discriminates."
